**1 [[Ribbo]] spawns after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Kill Star Peng with low DPH units (<65k) like [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]], [[Master of Selection Darvin (Special Cat)|Master of Selection Darvin]], and [[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Master of Logic Newtone]]. By doing this, you can start stacking spammable units on Ribbo's Barrier; it's not possible to stack many of the heavy-hitting Uber Rare options like [[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Supernova Cosmo]]. However, there's always the more humorous alternative of stacking unspeakable quantities of [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cats]], [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cats]], and/or [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cats]]. There's only one Commander Ostromeda, so your win condition is simply to kill it, and you can go about this in a variety of ways assuming you deal with Metal One Horn―bring [[Cheerleader Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Soba Cat]] or [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]] to that end, since all you need is one good Critical Hit.

Avoid letting [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] hit the enemy base if you're using him, since Spacefish Jones is positioned in such a way that instantly eviscerates Bahamut and prevents him from getting frozen by the [[Ototo Corps#Thunderbolt|Thunderbolt Cannon]]. Beyond that point, it's just a matter of bursting down all of its HP with your anti-Aliens of choice, and then cleaning up the mess thereafter. The leftover enemies cannot push through [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]], making them easy pickings for Newtone and Darvin, who will be off cooldown the entire time in the event that either of them die.

